<% content_for(:page_title) { "Metadata Quality — #{Netd.portal_name}" } %>
<div class="netd-page netd-faq netd-quality">
  <h1>Metadata Quality</h1>
  <p>How complete the metadata of the portal's theses and dissertations is, element by element, and how much of it comes from
    the institutions' own repositories. Measured against the <a href="https://ndltd.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/etd-ms-v1.1.html"
    target="_blank" rel="noopener">ETD-MS 1.1</a> metadata standard for theses and dissertations used by NDLTD, plus faculty,
    department and full text.</p>
  <% if @report.nil? || @report['institutions'].empty? %>
    <p class="netd-note">The quality report has not been computed yet. It is refreshed after every nightly harvest.</p>
  <% else %>
    <% all = @report['institutions'].first %>
    <%= render 'quality/legend' %>
    <table class="netd-stats netd-qheadline">
      <tr><td><%= all['etdms_compliance'] %>%</td><td>ETD-MS compliance at source: the mean share of the 12 ETD-MS elements that
        repositories supply in the proper metadata element</td></tr>
      <tr><td><%= all['complete_after_portal'] %>%</td><td>complete in the portal: the mean share of all 15 elements with a value,
        after the portal fills gaps from the full text</td></tr>
      <tr><td><%= number_with_delimiter(all['records']) %></td><td>ETDs from <%= @report['institutions_measured'] %> institutions</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h2>By element</h2>
    <p>Share of all ETDs in the portal, by where the value comes from. Hover over a bar for the figures.</p>
    <table class="netd-about netd-api netd-qtable">
      <thead><tr><th>Element <small>(ETD-MS)</small></th><th>Origin of the value</th>
        <% QualityReport::GROUPS.each_value do |(l, _)| %><th class="text-end"><%= l %></th><% end %></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      <% all['elements'].each do |e| %>
        <tr><td><%= e['label'] %><% if e['etdms'] %><br><small><code><%= e['etdms'] %></code></small><% end %></td>
          <td><%= quality_bar(e, e['label'], compact: false) %></td>
          <% QualityReport::GROUPS.each_key do |g| %><td class="text-end"><%= e[g] %>%</td><% end %></tr>
      <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>About these figures</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Computed after every nightly harvest; last computed <%= Time.parse(@report['generated_at']).in_time_zone(Netd.time_zone).strftime('%B %-d, %Y, %H:%M') %> (<%= Netd.time_zone_label %> time).
        Download: <%= link_to 'CSV', quality_path(format: :csv) %> · <%= link_to 'JSON', quality_path(format: :json) %>.</li>
      <li>"At source" counts only values the repository supplies in the proper metadata element. Values the portal reads from
        collection names or free text, or fills from the PDF (shown with a "derived" badge on record pages), make the portal
        more complete but do not help other services that harvest the repositories directly.</li>
      <li>Institutions that want to improve their metadata can contact <a href="mailto:<%= Netd.contact_email %>"><%= Netd.contact_email %></a>;
        the <%= link_to 'guide for institutions', contribute_path %> lists the recommended fields.</li>
    </ul>
  <% end %>
</div>
